# Driver-bot environment template for the `discord-live-round-trip`
# behavior test (Mission 23 Flight 3 Leg 3). Copy to `.env.hat` in this same
# directory (gitignored — see the repo `.gitignore`'s `*.env.hat` pattern)
# and fill in REAL values. NEVER commit real tokens; only this `.example`
# (placeholders only) is committed.
#
#   cp tests/behavior/.env.hat.example tests/behavior/.env.hat
#   # edit tests/behavior/.env.hat with real ids/token
#   set -a; . tests/behavior/.env.hat; set +a
#
# This flight simplifies the pre-reset `discord_hat` convention (N sender
# bot tokens, `THE_ONE_HAT_BOT_TOKENS`) down to ONE driver bot — the
# behavior test's apparatus only needs to post + read via REST, never to
# differentiate multiple senders.

# --- Driver bot token (the ACT+OBSERVE apparatus) ---
# A second Discord bot application, separate from the MAIN bot the
# connector under test connects as. See "Provisioning" below.
THE_ONE_HAT_DRIVER_TOKEN=replace-with-driver-bot-token

# --- Test guild + channels ---
THE_ONE_HAT_GUILD_ID=000000000000000000
# The channel the driver @mentions the main bot in (step 2/6).
THE_ONE_HAT_TEST_CHANNEL_ID=000000000000000001
# The channel the connector's `always_listen` config names (step 4).
THE_ONE_HAT_ALWAYS_LISTEN_CHANNEL_ID=000000000000000002
# A channel the connector does NOT track — proves silence (step 3).
THE_ONE_HAT_UNTRACKED_CHANNEL_ID=000000000000000003

# --- the-one's dev-instance base URL (optional; defaults per CLAUDE.md's
# behavior-test dev-instance conventions — port 8485, never 8484) ---
# THE_ONE_TEST_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8485

# ── Provisioning notes (carried over from the pre-reset discord_hat
# README's operational wisdom) ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Create BOTH bot applications in a REAL browser — never an automated one.
# The Discord Developer Portal requires hCaptcha during app creation and
# MFA-gated token resets; both hard-block automation.
#
#   1. https://discord.com/developers/applications -> New Application for
#      each bot (the MAIN bot the connector uses, and this DRIVER bot).
#   2. Bot tab -> Reset Token (MFA-gated) -> copy the token.
#   3. Intents: BOTH bots need Message Content intent enabled. The MAIN
#      bot reads inbound messages from the driver via the gateway; the
#      DRIVER bot reads the main bot's REPLIES back via REST
#      (`GET /channels/{id}/messages`), and Discord redacts `content` to
#      an empty string for any bot app without the intent — the old
#      "senders don't need it" advice assumed API-side assertions, not
#      this spec's REST observe path (learned live, 2026-09-01 run).
#   4. OAuth2 -> URL Generator: scope `bot`, permissions Send Messages +
#      Read Messages/View Channels for both bots. Authorize each into your
#      TEST guild (never a production guild).
